Let several servers share one cache directory

Each fetch wrote to partial/<key> and removed that directory first, and
the locks that kept two fetches of a key apart are per process. Two
servers given the same --cache-dir and asked for the same key at once
broke the entry: the second deleted the first one's half-unpacked
directory, the first renamed what it wrote afterwards into cache/,
where it counts as whole until it expires, and the second failed to
rename its own. Two servers fetching glibc's sources kept 17,162 of its
20,947 files, and gdb got 404 for the rest.

A fetch now writes to a directory of its own in partial/, and one that
finds the key already in cache/ when it is done uses that entry. An
entry being removed is moved into partial/ first, so a server killed
while deleting it leaves no partial entry in cache/, and cleanup sweeps
what killed servers left in partial/ once it is as old as an expired
entry.

